Orchestella quality / Phase 5 integrated local review build (2026-10-14)

Original host display codec, bounded service/sharing modules, guest display relay,
and optional profile controllers are Orchestella source under GNU GPL version 3
or later (GPL-3.0-or-later; root LICENSE and docs/adr/0014-licensing.md).
Public GPL reference source was inspected for architecture and permissions;
no reference implementation was copied into these host modules.

Guest packages are optional, fetched only following explicit profile selection
through signed distribution repositories. labwc, wayvnc, Mesa, fonts, Podman,
rootless helpers and Docker CLI remain independent guest programs; their licenses
and corresponding source are supplied by the selected distribution.

Optional code-server 4.141.0 is an independent guest service under MIT License.
It is not bundled in this APK. The official ARM64 input, SHA-256 and ABI constraints
are locked in guest-assets/features/inputs.json. Its included LICENSE/third-party
notices remain in the verified installation. This build does not install or
redistribute the proprietary Microsoft VS Code Server, enable a cloud tunnel,
or create third-party identities.

Packaged kernel and QEMU retain their pre-existing GPL-2.0 notices and build input
records. Their runtime binaries are unchanged; the independently compiled guest
agent is updated with its matching source and manifest. This is a local review
artifact, not a published release. A public release still requires exact
corresponding-source delivery and the project release gates.

API-26 core library desugaring uses com.android.tools:desugar_jdk_libs:2.1.5,
maintained by Google; dependency licenses are preserved in the build input
records. Desktop CPU-copy, AVF/GPU, USB/SAF and IDE runtime validation levels are
recorded separately in the Phase 5 verification matrix. No hardware acceleration
or zero-copy claim follows from host EGL initialization or JVM tests.
